Open GH_BROWSER from wasip1, including when stdin is a pipe.

Reason: gh auth login --web still has to open the device URL when stdin is
not a terminal (yes | gh auth login -w). go-gh starts GH_BROWSER with
os/exec, which cannot spawn on wasip1, and the non-interactive path only
prints the URL. This sends the command through gh_host instead.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).
removeWhen: wasip1 can spawn, and gh opens GH_BROWSER without a TTY.

diff --git a/internal/authflow/flow.go b/internal/authflow/flow.go
--- a/internal/authflow/flow.go
+++ b/internal/authflow/flow.go
@@ -68,8 +68,15 @@
 			}
 
 			if !isInteractive {
-				fmt.Fprintf(w, "%s to continue in your web browser: %s\n", cs.Bold("Open this URL"), authURL)
-				return nil
+				// A pipe (yes | gh auth login -w) is not a TTY, so upstream
+				// only prints the URL. Still hand it to GH_BROWSER. The
+				// printed URL remains for when that command fails.
+				fmt.Fprintf(w, "%s to continue in your web browser: %s\n", cs.Bold("Open this URL"), authURL)
+				if err := b.Browse(authURL); err != nil {
+					fmt.Fprintf(w, "%s Failed opening a web browser at %s\n", cs.Red("!"), authURL)
+					fmt.Fprintf(w, "  %s\n", err)
+				}
+				return nil
 			}
 
 			fmt.Fprintf(w, "%s to open %s in your browser... ", cs.Bold("Press Enter"), authURL)
